Description:
    Installs the two tables ActiveJob::Durable writes to
    (active_job_durable_runs and active_job_durable_steps). Two files are
    generated; apply the one that fits the application's database setup:

    Single database (the tables live next to the application's tables):
        run the generated migration, bin/rails db:migrate, and delete
        db/durable_schema.rb.

    Separate database: add a "durable" database to config/database.yml with
    "migrations_paths: db/durable_migrate", point the record class at it,

        # config/initializers/active_job_durable.rb
        ActiveJob::Durable.connects_to = { database: { writing: :durable } }

    run bin/rails db:prepare (which loads db/durable_schema.rb), and delete
    the generated migration.

Example:
    bin/rails generate ajdc:install

    This will create:
        db/durable_schema.rb
        db/migrate/TIMESTAMP_create_active_job_durable_tables.rb
